            <div xml:id="d701">

                <pb facs="0782" n="770" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg770"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853i.79682/1: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-12-24T12:00:00-00:44">December 24,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 24—11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. President Barclay approved today contract between Liberian Government and
                    Pan-American Airways to start operation of air mail services within a year from
                    Liberia to Portuguese Guinea connecting with other air mail services to Europe,
                    United States and other countries. Company has been granted limited monopoly as
                    against other American companies for a term of 10 years.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
